WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
Spy Hunter, the arcade smash of the 80s comes home.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:26.960
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.920
I'm Mike.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.420
I'm Joe. I'm Sam.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.720
And I'm Sean. Alright guys, and today we are talking about...

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.880
Spy Hunter!

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.600
Spy Hunter!

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:42.440
Spy Hunter. Spy Hunter, the video game, based on the arcade game, based on the James Bond movie series.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.220
And that's probably why you guys were laughing like that, right?

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.580
Yeah. Like what? Yeah.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.140
Like, oh, okay, cool.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:56.080
This was first released in 1983 by Bally Midway, which I think now is just Midway?

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.280
No, but back then it was Bally Midway.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.040
Oh, I mean like did they just turn into Midway?

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.200
Yes, I think that's what happened.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.660
Oh, okay. And now it's on the NES in September of 1987.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.800
Neat. Still published by Bally Midway, so this is our first game from them.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.920
Good. Does anybody remember anything about Midway?

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.520
I know they did some games that I liked.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.380
Yeah, I remember Midway popping up a lot.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.440
So you're fond of it.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.100
So maybe you'll be fond of the game.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.860
You said you remember it, so you're fond of it.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.040
Yeah. So you dated the president's wife, right?

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.440
That's true. Oh, that was it.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.720
It's like such a weird...

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.680
You dated the president's wife.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.120
Well, going back to Spy Hunter...

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.740
It's the first overhead car game on the NES, right?

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.620
Like top down.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.980
Yeah. That's cool.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.920
It was like Legend of Zelda on rails.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.180
Uh... Because Legend of Zelda is like top down and now you are in a car.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.960
Okay. I think that's like the best way to give like an overview of what this game is.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.320
Well, it's not like Legend of Zelda at all.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.240
It's basically Legend of Zelda.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.720
Sam, would you like to talk about what Spy Hunter is?

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.800
Give like an overview of how you play the game?

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.880
Yes. So go ahead.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:10.680
All right. So the way you play this game is you drive in your little secret agent, very speedy car,

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:14.000
and you can fire guns out of your car.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:20.820
Uh... And you're just trying to survive and not run into stuff, stay on the highway, shoot things

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:26.000
as they come, not get hit, bumped off the road by the armored cars, not get shot by the

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.760
helicopter. Try not to kill civilians.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.100
Try... Try.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.460
Whatever. Um...

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:36.460
Uh... And also jump back into your, uh, your...

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.360
Like what the...

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.100
Like the tractor trailer that you came out of.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.940
Mm-hmm. So that's how you get your, uh, your upgraded weapons.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.180
Yeah. Uh...

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.820
And then that helps you fend off all these guys.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.620
And you're just trying to survive and rack up a high score.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.280
And I think that was a wonderful way to describe the game.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:54.260
I think that's pretty clear. Just want to mention that it's also, it's pretty fast paced.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.580
Oh, yeah. Very fast paced. Much faster than I thought it was going to be.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:59.660
Yep. So I think that's a great overview of the game.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.220
And now we can kind of just go into our first impressions.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.580
Because I think for a lot of us, even though this is a, definitely what I would consider

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.720
an arcade hit, uh, and has been iterated on a lot.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:11.560
This is some of our first times playing Spy Hunter.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:13.200
So I'd love to hear some first impressions.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:20.440
Well, my first impression is, uh, I had played the remake, uh, almost two decades ago now,

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.400
I think. Um, there was a 2002, maybe?

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.400
Maybe 2001? PlayStation 2 game?

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.640
Uh, that was just, I think, a remake of this game.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.560
And it was called Spy Hunter?

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.420
It was called Spy Hunter.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:38.060
Okay. Um, it, it still had the cool white car that could turn into a boat.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.760
Um, it still, like, ended levels by, um,

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.280
going into the, uh, weapons van.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.720
Um, it was, uh, I think a pretty decent retelling, I guess.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.000
It's not, not like there's a story.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.840
I mean, there was a story in the remake.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.460
Yeah, it was just called Spy Hunter.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.480
Yeah, it was, uh, I, I have pretty fond memories of it.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.140
Because it was one of the first PS2 games that I owned.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.520
And, uh, it had some pretty cool effects when you turn into, like, the boat and stuff.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.320
Um, it had a mission structure.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.500
It had a story.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.920
Um, all of that doesn't really exist in this one.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.740
It's just, uh, go as fast as you can.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:22.140
Uh, because you can go faster, um, uh, than you should in this game.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.120
And, uh, just kill a bunch of dudes.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.920
And forever. Sure.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:26.780
The road doesn't end.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.480
Right. Um, there's no, there's no, like, hooray, you beat the game.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.080
He's on highway one.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.520
Yeah, you're on. Yeah.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.860
And, uh, yeah, you just sort of like do that gameplay loop for a while.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:40.480
Maybe jump into the boat if you want to.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.780
But, yeah, it's, it's, it's fine.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.980
Okay. Sam, first impressions?

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:50.160
Uh, first impressions were that, okay, it's kind of like, it's kind of like Mock Rider

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.000
a little bit.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:56.460
And it, since this came out, I guess, before Mock Rider, I guess Mock Rider would be a little

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.920
bit like this. So, it's cool that you get that inspiration from it.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.020
And you can see that there's the, the pad, like the, what, the water pad, the puddles

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.800
on the ground that are slick.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.860
And there's, you're shooting with your car.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.540
And it, I think it did feel a lot like Mock Rider.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.020
Uh, like, it's very fast.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.580
Even in concept of like, you know.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.640
Some people you want to pass, other people you want to bump off the road.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.360
Um, and I thought that it was also very easy to die.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.360
Okay. Like, very easy to die.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.980
And did you think that was something that you eventually learned to overcome?

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.700
Yeah. I think so. Okay. I think it's something that the more you play it.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:31.740
Yeah. Yep.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.680
Joe? Yeah.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:37.020
When I, when I first started playing it, the speed of it kind of threw me off a little

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:41.380
bit. Cause I, I feel like, maybe it's just me, but it feels faster than, than Mock Rider

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:45.400
or, uh, you know, any, any, really any of these other games that we've played.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:52.040
Um, but I think that really, other than, other than that, I think just the fact that it's

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.780
very simple, but it works very well.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.640
So I, you know, I thought it was good.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:59.200
Yeah. And I think that's my first dimension too, is it's a great arcade game.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.360
It, it, it, the loop is nice.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:07.080
The, um, the fact that it doesn't interrupt your flow by being like, oh, you beat this

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.440
stage. Now go to the next.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.540
Like the fact that it is just kind of endless and you're racking up a score.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.440
It's perfect for that arcade arcadey thing.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.000
Uh, you know, I don't know if that's like something you need at the home.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.820
Like that's something that I always focus on with the NES is like, what does this do?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:27.800
Like now that you can have it in your living room, like, you know, not that, not saying

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.320
that that affects like how I feel about the gameplay, but just maybe affects how I feel

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.740
about like now on the NES, like what's different.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:36.480
Is it just a inferior version of the arcade thing?

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:37.360
Who's to say?

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:42.480
Uh, I think we can talk now a little bit about just the, can I actually challenge you on one

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:46.740
thing? Um, the fact that this game just goes on forever.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:53.680
I think that that is a problem that there's no like end goal aside from, you know, your

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.300
high score, because I thought we, we've, we've brought up a lot of times how we were

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.000
sort of past this, um, by this point.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.840
I think, I think that's what I was saying.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:05.800
If, if I wasn't clear, I think I was saying is like, that's great and all for an arcade

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.580
game. What is it bringing now that it's on the NES?

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:13.360
You know? So I'm saying like, my first impression is great arcade game, but like, how quickly am

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:17.600
I going to get tired? I thought you said that like, it's better now that you don't have to like put another

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.700
quarter. No, sorry.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:22.840
Yeah. So I guess I, what I meant to say is like, you know, now that I have access to it in

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:25.500
my living room, whenever, how, how much do I care about it?

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:29.120
You know? Because it's like, it's not just like this pick up and play experience.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.820
It's kind of like, it's, you know, I'm just playing for points.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.060
All right. The points don't matter.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.240
It's who wants it anyway.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:37.140
You know, it's like, well, let's, let's, let's go to where you wanted to go.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:41.160
Okay, cool. So I think I'd like to just talk, you know, since we talked a little bit about how the

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:46.180
game controls, how you felt about, you know, all the different weapons that you had available

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:50.600
to you, how the enemies came at you, just kind of like, you know, your gameplay experience

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:53.420
and whether the game was fair to you or not.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:59.940
I, I liked the, there were only a few different weapons, but at first I liked them until I

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.800
kind of, I kind of thought, so you have the oil slick.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:07.000
Yep. Which puts a straight line of oil behind you and any car that passes, it veers off the road

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.660
and crashes. And you have, what is it?

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:09.760
The smoke screen. Smoke screen.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.080
Which makes them stop, right?

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.660
They'd stop in their tracks because they can't see.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:20.460
They can't see. I suppose. Um, and then you have the missiles, which only, as far as I was able to tell, only let

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:21.680
you shoot helicopters.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:25.860
That's correct. I, I didn't think helicopters were that difficult to deal with otherwise.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.400
So like it, it sucks when you got dodged, helicopters attacked, but they kind of telegraph

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:36.060
them anyways. Um, but the, uh, the other two, the, the oil slick and the smoke screen, even though they

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:40.200
make the cars do something different, they really both fundamentally do the same thing.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.440
They stop anything that's behind you.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.540
Like there's nothing, there's not really a power up that gets things in front of you

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.160
or like does something with speed or does anything like that unique or interesting.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:54.200
Right. And I, yeah, I think I would have liked to have seen more power ups than three, but I will

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.700
say that like, I enjoyed the oil one.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.100
Me too. You know, like laying out oil for people behind me.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:01.520
It felt like you were, especially because you know, the big thing about this game is

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.420
that you kind of have like gears.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:08.360
So you, you know, if you hit up on the D pad, you'll get faster and faster and you can

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:11.540
simultaneously slow down if you need to by hitting down on the D pad.

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:16.020
And I just thought that it was like really cool to speed past somebody, lay down some

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.560
oil, watch them slick off to the side of the road.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.900
And then it's like, okay, I'm going to deal with what's next in front of me.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:28.760
You know? Right. I liked, I liked when you actually felt in control of the car doing cool action movie

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:29.600
style things.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:36.660
Yeah. I hated when it was just like me spamming the, you know, the turrets that are on the front

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.660
of my car that I presume I'm using to shoot at the cars.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:44.880
I hated when it was just that and I'm just shooting at things in front of me because, because

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:51.940
it is top down, that's not very like dynamic and is more like a shmup style thing.

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:56.180
Yeah. That doesn't translate here because you can only be on the road, you know?

00:09:56.360 --> 00:10:00.320
So you're kind of like more focusing on like your driving and then you are on your shooting.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.360
And so I like better using the power ups.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:06.600
And I kind of wish that that was just the focus in general, but like all these creative

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:10.060
ways to kill as opposed to, well, you always have your guns.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:16.340
Yeah. I think that also the, the guns can be a little bit annoying because if you shoot someone,

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:21.460
it's like their car breaks down before it like explodes and disappears or whatever.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:22.840
So you can run into them and die.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.000
That is okay.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.500
So I'm glad you brought that up.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:29.300
It's like, I think that, I guess that's part of the skill of it and like swerving around

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:35.400
them. Because I think that the fact that the game doesn't hide like the full speed that it can

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.980
go behind like, I don't know, like another pickup could have been like a turbo.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.740
So instead of just, that's your max speed.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.360
You can do that for as long as you want.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:48.820
It is actually, I don't have the Twitch capabilities to play at the max speed.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.240
I don't think anyone's supposed to.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.360
I was rarely at the max speed.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:52.700
Yeah. Because I would die immediately.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:57.760
I know. And, but my lizard brain just had go faster, go faster.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.960
And I just kept wanting to go faster.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.320
Don't acknowledge the lizard brain.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:07.880
I just wanted to keep going faster because that's just what you do in games.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:09.360
You try and go as fast as you can.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:16.680
But I had to like actually consciously stop myself and go like at the, like near the speed

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.300
limit. And it just felt odd.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:21.040
But even in my, and I know what you're talking about.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:22.700
Cause like even in modern games, right?

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:27.140
When you're like, let's say it's like a challenge mode thing in a certain game and you have to

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:31.320
do a specific thing and you get really far along, but then you do something that like

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.240
fails the challenge.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.660
You have to start back at a certain point.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.700
Your immediate instinct is just like, okay, I've already done this part.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.280
So I'm just going to rush through this as fast as possible.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:41.880
And sometimes you make very careless mistakes that make you restart even earlier than you

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:42.860
got the previous time.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:44.840
That's what it is for Spy Hunter with me too.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:48.740
It's like, I know I shouldn't be going fast, but I want to, I want to go fast.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.340
Like, you know, I really just want to go it.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:55.600
And like, I'm not saying I got, I definitely got better at the max speed as it went on.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:12:00.040
Like I was dying immediately on the max speed when I started and I didn't get better.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:05.440
But by no means is that like, did Bally Midway think like, this is how you're supposed

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.900
to play the game is like a good player.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:08.500
We'll just be at the max speed the whole time.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:11.020
And they'll just be shooting the enemies and clicking the power ups as they go.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:16.120
It's meant, there's a reason why there's gears and you're meant to slow down the

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.480
turns. You're meant to speed up on the straightaways.

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.760
It's, it's cool. And I like that touch.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:24.980
I think that's one thing that I can say is that controlling the car felt great.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:31.880
Yeah. It was just not what, it was not an intuitive thing for me at the beginning.

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:37.560
And maybe there should have been a cap on like, that the max speed shouldn't have been

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.440
like breakneck.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:42.480
I don't know. Maybe, I mean, it's, it's cool though, when you have those little stretches, I think it's

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:46.980
good that it's in there. It's just maybe, I wasn't, I wasn't smart enough to know immediately.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:52.520
And especially later on as I kept using like all the gears, it was kind of cool to like

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:57.860
slow down on, on, on like a, on a dime, you know, like super fast, slow down, shoot a

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.100
car and then immediately start speeding up again.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:01.280
You know, like I did like that.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:05.920
It wasn't like realistic gear changes where it was going to take me a while to get fast.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.680
It was, it felt like it was very smooth actually.

